## Summary

Implemented the native **SwiftUI / Apple HIG `DriveScorePage`** at full web parity (`web/src/features/driving/pages/DriveScorePage.tsx`, route `/drive-score`), adaptive across macOS + iOS.

**Parity: 160/160** — 29 panels + 12 charts + 3 states + 116 strings, all bound to an `@Observable` `DriveScorePageModel` (no networking in the view, ADR-004). The web `scoreDrive` algorithm and every aggregation (averages, trend, category bars, histogram, period stats, best/worst, achievements, tips) are ported into a deterministic, unit-tested `DriveScoreEngine`. SI stays canonical in the model; conversion happens only at the render boundary via the shared KMP `Units` facade (ADR-005). Charts use the P3 Swift Charts wrappers (no WKWebView).

**Files:** 14 new source + 2 test files under `Sources/Features/Driving/` & `Tests/Unit/Features/Driving/`; nav alias `/drive-score` → `.driving` + route registration; +115 `driveScore.*` xcstrings (additive); 2 ledger rows; evidence log.

**Verification (all green):**
- `swiftlint --strict` = 0, `swiftformat --lint` = 0/16, placeholder scan COUNT=0/EXIT=0
- In-scope whole-module type-check (built the real Kotlin/Native `Shared.xcframework` via Gradle) — **0 DriveScore errors on macOS AND iOS targets** (all 14 files, incl. `#if os(iOS)` branches)
- Executable logic harness: **69/69 checks pass** — and it caught + fixed 2 real latent bugs (`Hashable`/`Sendable` on types holding `LocalizedStringKey`; `Double % Int`)
- Full `xcodebuild` = RED (exit 65), honestly reported as **pre-existing out-of-scope** `#Preview`/toolchain drift in ~29 untouched `TeslaSync/*` files — the identical condition the already-DONE sibling `StatisticsPage` documents.

**Key reconciliation:** files live in `Sources/Features/Driving/` (the only group `project.yml` compiles), not the prompt's nominal `TeslaSync/Features/Driving/` — matching how every sibling parity page resolves this. Committed as `ed42a3f9`. **EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE.**

